# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit the real .env (see .gitignore).
#
# This file lists environment variables our scripts read directly. It is
# NOT the same thing as DSH's own credential store ($DSH_HOME/.credentials.yaml
# or $DSH_HOME/.env) — see README.md "Segurança" for why the distinction
# matters: DeepSeek Harness's Claude Code / Codex subagent providers scrub
# credential-shaped variables from the child process env unless our profile
# config explicitly forwards them, so setting ANTHROPIC_API_KEY/OPENAI_API_KEY
# here does NOT make Claude/Codex use paid API billing by itself.

# --- Relay providers (DeepSeek primary, OpenAI fallback) ---
# These power only the small DSH "brain" that delegates to Claude/Codex. They
# are unrelated to the child products' own subscription authentication.
VERAMUX_DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
#VERAMUX_DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat

# Optional fallback. This key is used only by the OpenAI relay route and is
# never forwarded to the DeepSeek endpoint or to the Codex reviewer child.
VERAMUX_OPENAI_API_KEY=
#VERAMUX_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5-mini

# --- Optional: override DSH's home directory (default: ~/.dsh) ---
#DSH_HOME=

# --- Optional: override the P2 run-journal/lock state directory
# (default: ${XDG_STATE_HOME:-~/.local/state}/agent-stack) ---
#AGENT_STATE_HOME=

# --- Doctor risk detection (leave unset unless you know you need them) ---
# If either of these is set in your shell, `agent doctor` will warn/block:
# it does not mean Claude/Codex will silently bill against it (see above),
# but it is a known footgun for other tools and for future misconfiguration.
#ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
